This is an Azure alias record, not a literal IP address. Enable the alias option
and select the target Azure resource. The original IP value was shown as "-".

## Azure-managed Records: Reference Only

Azure creates the root NS and SOA records automatically. If the zone is recreated,
use its newly assigned nameservers at your domain registrar, not this old list.

### NS Record

Name: @
Type: NS
TTL: 172800

- ns1-08.azure-dns.com.
- ns2-08.azure-dns.net.
- ns3-08.azure-dns.org.
- ns4-08.azure-dns.info.

